{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA/update: duplicate-title detection already existed only as per-call duplicate_warning from recent-creates; creation volume existed only implicitly as raw CREATE events / reconciler per-pass create counts. Neither produced an aggregate observer metric, so mass creation was silent unless a human saw each advisory/log line. The implemented fix adds independent read-only store metrics for rolling-hour duplicate-title excess and rolling-hour CREATE volume, using the same normalize_title rule as duplicate_warning, suppressing documented distinct-file-impact and recurring bridge-alert false positives, returning measured zeroes for empty windows, and leaving bridge/enrichment queues out of the signal path. RED: pytest tests/unit/metrics/test_event_metrics.py -q failed on missing duplicate_title_peak_hour/create_volume_peak_hour before production changes. Verification: targeted tests passed; historical replay fired duplicate detector for 2026-08-31/09-01 and volume detector for 2026-09-04/05 while baseline 2026-08-20..25 stayed below threshold; make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=8 passed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788861373151419001,"uuid":"6d4ac57e-dd23-45f6-92d3-7e638abfd1bf"}